Subject: [PATCH 0/2] arm64: dts: allwinner: h700: Add Anbernic RG34XX SP

The Anbernic RG34XX SP is an Allwinner H700 clamshell handheld. Its
board follows the RG35XX SP (same PMIC, keys, lid sensor and Wi-Fi/BT
wiring), and adds two analog sticks with stick-click buttons, wired as on
the RG35XX H. This series adds its compatible and a device tree that
includes the RG35XX SP tree and adds:

- the analog sticks (GPADC channel 0 behind a 4-way analog mux, as on
  the RG35XX H), polled every 16 ms
- the stick-click buttons on PE8/PE9
- the battery values from the vendor device tree, including its 4.10 V
  charge voltage limit

Not described yet: the 3.4" 720x480 RGB/SPI panel and its backlight
(they need the H616 display engine, TCON and PWM series still under
review), and a rumble motor, which the vendor tree names but which is
not confirmed on this model. As in the upstream RG35XX trees, only the
first of the two microSD slots is described.

